    "intro_narrative": "The year is 2142. The surface world has been reduced to a toxic wasteland by the Great Collapse, leaving only scattered remnants of advanced technology buried deep within subterranean bunkers. You are a lone Scavenger, braving the irradiated ruins in search of the fabled Genesis Bunker. Your primary life-support suit is failing, and you desperately need to synchronize it with the planetary orbital array to survive the approaching hyper-storm. Your objective is clear: extract the master timezone data to recalibrate your systems. You have managed to pry open the heavy blast doors of an abandoned laboratory, a room filled with offline machinery, tangled cables, and dormant terminals. You must reactivate these ancient devices, understand how they interconnect, and restore their functions to synthesize the chronometer needed to save your life. The ambient hum of failing generators adds to the tension. Time is running out, and this rusted machinery is your only hope for survival.",
    "narrative_style": "post_apocalyptic"
